# Code Blocks Full Test

## 1. Python (basic)

```python
print("Hello, World!")
x = 42
```

## 2. Python with title

```python {title="app.py"}
def greet(name):
    return f"Hello, {name}!"

print(greet("Markup+"))
```

## 3. HTML with Preview

```html {title="page.html"}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        body { font-family: sans-serif; padding: 20px; }
        .box {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #7c3aed, #ec4899);
            color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="box">
        <h1>Hello, Markup+!</h1>
        <p>This is a live preview.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

## 4. CSS with Preview

```css {title="style.css"}
h1 {
    color: #7c3aed;
    font-size: 32px;
}
button {
    background: #7c3aed;
    color: white;
    padding: 10px 20px;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    cursor: pointer;
}
button:hover {
    background: #5b21b6;
}
```

## 5. JavaScript with Preview

```javascript {title="app.js"}
const name = "Markup+";
console.log("Hello, " + name);
console.log("2 + 2 =", 2 + 2);
console.log("Done!");
```

## 6. Bash (no preview)

```bash
pip install markup-plus
mup examples/code.mup
```

## 7. With Line Numbers and Highlight

```python {title="advanced.py" linenos hl=[3,7]}
import asyncio
from dataclasses import dataclass

@dataclass
class User:
    name: str
    email: str

async def fetch_users():
    await asyncio.sleep(1)
    return [User("Ali", "ali@example.com")]
```

